meta {
  name: 05 - Delete
  seq: 5
}

docs {
  Two deletion mechanisms:

  - **Soft Delete Document** - flips the `deleted` flag on the Mongo record; everything
    else (record, revision history, MinIO content, vector store chunks) is left in place,
    and the flag propagates to the indexed chunks asynchronously so search stops
    surfacing the document. There is no API-level undo.
  - **Delete Document** (hard delete) - tears down a document entirely: terminates its
    Temporal workflow, deletes all vector store chunks, removes every version's object
    from MinIO (`{{documentId}}/*` prefix, not just the latest), deletes the Mongo
    document, and deletes its revision history.
}
